Sure.  But which of these do you go after first?

-- The captain
-- The jabberwock
-- The minotaur
-- The magical eye
-- The cockatrice
-- The master mind flayer

Now, this is obviously a pretty nasty 'summon nasties', given that it
just happens to pick out all the stuff you're able to get chewed up
badly by -- especially in combination.  But it'll serve to illustrate
the point.  What's bad about each of these?

-- The captain hits hard, doesn't respect E, and may have gloves; if he
does, he _will_ pick up a cockatrice corpse.
-- The jabberwock hits hard and often.
-- The minotaur hits hard and doesn't respect E.
-- The magical eye can cast 'slow' and 'stun', and will step back.
-- The cockatrice's attack triggers stoning one time out of ten, 
regardless of MC factor, MR, or anything else.
-- The MMF will cause amnesia and if you're a low-INT character,
possibly even an instakill.

So yes.. you can kill the cockatrice in one turn, but in that list, it
ranks as next-to-last to kill... slightly more important than the
jabberwock.  Most 'summon nasties' aren't _this_ nasty, but this still
kind of points up why footrices should still be considered "nasty".

