Have you tried doing this in Spork recently?  :)
A couple things don't make this quite the cakewalk that vanilla is.  

First, there is no "Swing Dead Thing" skill -- this means that you are 
effectively Restricted in cockatrice corpse.  This also means that you 
will hit no more than 75% of the time, despite any rings of increase 
accuracy, luck, level, etc. etc. ad nauseam.

Second, since Elbereth is no longer 100% effective, you can't handle the
situation above the way you would in vanilla (burn E, kill the captain,
kill the footrice, stone the rest).  My prediction for what happens if
you try to kill the footrice first in the above situation:

-- You kill the footrice in one hit, x% chance of a corpse.
-- The magical eye slows you and possibly stuns you as well.
-- The hitty monsters (J, H) hit you.
-- The mind flayer hits you and removes the grease from your helmet.
-- The captain flips a coin and either hits you or steps to the corpse.

Next turn, you ... wait, you don't get a turn.  You're slowed.

-- The magical eye is speed 6 and doesn't get a turn either.
-- The hitty monsters hit you.
-- The mind flayer induces amnesia and grabs some INT points.
-- The captain either picks up the corpse or just keeps hitting you if
there's no corpse.

At this point you should get a turn, but you now have a major, major
problem on your hands -- you're slowed, maybe stunned, and two instakill
monsters (captain with a c corpse and mind flayer) are standing next to
you.

So while it's still quite possible to use a footrice to bash your way
out of summon storms, it's not going to be quite the no-brainer it is in
vanilla.  :)  Which I kind of like, honestly.

